    "subscription": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "One per child and plan; parent_id denormalised for 'my subscriptions' lists. Status machine pending_payment/matching/active/paused/past_due/cancelled is enforced by the core service. period_* are UTC instants of the billing period. preferred_slots is JSON text [{weekday 1-7, start_minute, end_minute}] in Africa/Kampala wall-clock minutes (same convention as availability_slot). No unique (child) because a child may hold several subscriptions; duplicates are a core-service check."
    },
    "match_request": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "type new|rematch|substitute (SR 7.2/7.3); session_id is set for substitute requests. attempts counts offers made; after 5 failures status becomes admin_queue. Teachers already rematched away from a child are derived from assignments with end_reason rematch_requested."
    },
    "match_offer": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "Sequential offers (SR 7.2). rank is the position, rank_score is integer basis points 0-10000 (no floats), score_breakdown is JSON text {factor: basis points, weights_version} for transparency and tuning. active_key = '<match_request_id>:<teacher_id>' while response is pending, null once resolved or soft-deleted: unique index = one active offer per teacher per request, offers are idempotent."
    },
    "assignment": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "Current teacher-child pairing. start_at/end_at UTC; is_trial marks a trial pairing; end_reason set when it ends. active_key = '<child_id>:<subscription_id>' while end_at is null and not soft-deleted: one active assignment per child per subscription (a trial counts; converting ends the trial with end_reason trial_converted and creates the regular one)."
    },
    "session": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "Status is an enum of exactly the SR 7.4 states; allowed transitions are enforced by the core service, not the schema (reference table: appwrite/session_rules.py ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS). Overlap rule: Appwrite has no exclusion constraint, so the core service checks the teacher's sessions for time overlap in the write path (session_rules.create_session) and the unique index on teacher_slot_key ('<teacher_id>|<UTC start>' while the session holds the slot, null for cancelled/no_show/void/soft-deleted) is the backstop for concurrent requests with the same start. Deviation from the ticket wording: derived key instead of raw (teacher_id, scheduled_start_at) so a cancelled session does not block re-booking the slot (soft-delete/unique convention). Substitute: a NEW session row for the same slot, is_substitute true, substitute_for_session_id = the session the teacher cancelled, assignment_id null. Indexes: by_teacher_day (teacher sessions by day), by_child_period (child sessions by period), by_status_changed (auto-confirmation job). Residual risk: the unique teacher_slot_key only catches the same start; two overlapping sessions with different starts can both insert, so the core service (W01 #97 / S01 #93) must serialise writes per teacher or re-check after insert. S01 (#93) generation identity: slot_ref = '<ISO weekday>-<start minute>:<Africa/Kampala local date>' (never changes, even if the session is rescheduled); generation_key = '<assignment_id>:<slot_ref>', a derived unique key that stays set while the row exists (cancelled, no_show and void rows keep it, so the nightly job never recreates them) and is nulled only by soft delete (cancel_future, rollback after a lost overlap race), so the slot can be generated again. Restore recomputes it (hs_core.scheduling.rules.restore_session_patch). is_trial marks the first session of a trial pairing (MAT-6). overridden = a parent/teacher reschedule moved the session: the generator never prunes or moves it."
    },
    "session_checkin": {
      "deletion": "immutable",
      "note": "Insert-only evidence. lat_e6/lng_e6 integer micro-degrees (M01 convention), accuracy_m metres, device_time_at is the device clock, server_time_at is authoritative (VRF), distance_m to the home pin computed server-side, within_geofence null when not computed, flagged requires parent confirmation to count. Unique (session_id, type): one check-in and one check-out per session."
    },
    "session_confirmation": {
      "deletion": "immutable",
      "note": "Parent response after check-out; auto_confirmed true when the hourly job confirms after 48 h without dispute (responded_by_id then null). One per session."
    },
    "cancellation": {
      "deletion": "immutable",
      "note": "One per cancelled session. by_role parent|teacher|admin; is_late decides cancelled_by_parent_late vs cancelled_by_parent_ontime on the session (threshold is a core-service setting)."
    },
    "dispute": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "Raised by the parent after check-out (SR 7.4 disputed -> confirmed|void). open_key = session_id while status is not resolved, null after resolution or soft-delete: one open dispute per session."
    }
